Z||000023||DiggityDan||06-11-2000||09:19 PM||||Haze.........first of all, Price will be determined by how many people end up getting in on this with us. We only need a couple more to get 10 people committed for a 15% discount. <BR>Good question on the shipping, as far as that goes I am not for sure. That all depends on how Lawrence sends them and how much the kit weighs. Lawrence.......any guestimates on shipping. <BR>Right now there is no cut off on the order date. I will set one when (a) we get at least 10 people commited or (b) I feel like we won't get the 10 commited people. Either way, when I set the day I will give everyone a week or so to get with me to join up. I want to make sure everyone has a chance to join in on this that wants to but I also don't want anyone to have to wait too long to get their kits.<BR>Lawrence, I guess me and you need to talk alittle, so if you could e-mail me at diggity_dan@hotmail.com or give me your e-mail, we can work out the final details.<BR>Again, if you want in on this............e-mail me to get on the list.<BR>Thanks again <BR>Dan||||reg||1
Z||000024||lawrence||06-12-2000||08:15 PM||||Dan,<P>As for shipping, individual boxes are $7 each.  That's second day, with insurance.<P>If I send a couple to an address, then the shipping should be about $10.  If I send 10 kits, shipping is likely to be $30.  Sorry I can't be more specific, but if it's within a couple dollars, we'll let it slide.<P>How many people are interested so far?<P>-L<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe/sts" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe/sts</A>  - Sequential Turn Signals||||reg||1
